#!/bin/sh
# Sync the GNOME color-scheme with noctalia's theme mode, so that every app
# that follows the xdg-desktop-portal appearance setting (ghostty, firefox/zen,
# electron apps, nvim's auto-dark-mode, ...) flips together.
#
# Called from noctalia hooks:
#   theme_mode_changed  NOCTALIA_THEME_MODE=dark|light is set by the shell
#   started             no env; ask the running shell for the resolved mode
#
# dconf writes the key directly and needs no schema lookup, so this works from
# noctalia's bare hook environment without guessing store paths.
set -eu

mode="${NOCTALIA_THEME_MODE:-${1:-}}"
if [ -z "$mode" ]; then
  mode="$(noctalia msg theme-mode-get 2>/dev/null || true)"
fi

case "$mode" in
  dark | true) scheme="prefer-dark" ;;
  light | false) scheme="prefer-light" ;;
  *) exit 0 ;;
esac

dconf write /org/gnome/desktop/interface/color-scheme "'$scheme'"
